text:
Object Oriented Analysis and Design Using Java
Abstraction
Abstract class in Java:
• The class has to be declared as abstract if it contains at least one abstract method.
• An abstract class does not allow you to create objects of its type. In this case, we can
only use the objects of its subclass.
• Using an abstract class, we can achieve 0 to 100% abstraction.
• There is always a default constructor in an abstract class, it can also have a
parameterized constructor.
• The abstract class can also contain final and static methods.

Object Oriented Analysis and Design Using Java
Abstraction : Example
Output:
The Dog says: bow bow
Zzz
abstract class Animal {   // Abstract class
public abstract void animalSound();  // Abstract method
public void sleep() {                // Regular method
System.out.println("Zzz");
}
}
class Dog extends Animal {               // Subclass
@Override
public void animalSound() {
System.out.println("The dog says: bow bow");
}
}
class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
Dog myDog = new Dog();            // Create a Dog object
myDog.animalSound();
myDog.sleep();
}
}

